# Legends of the Twins — the cutlass (p.16), magic items (pp.27-29, p.120) and artifacts (pp.29-31).
Cutlass	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Cutlass	TYPE:Weapon.Melee.Martial.Standard.Slashing.Piercing.Sword	COST:12	WT:3	DAMAGE:1d6	CRITRANGE:2	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	SPROP:A short, heavy shipboard blade that both slashes and pierces. Light. Its basket hilt gives the wielder a +2 circumstance bonus to avoid being disarmed. Damage 1d4 (Small), 1d6 (Medium).	SOURCEPAGE:p.16
Astrolabe of Quantifiable Foresight	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:8300	WT:4	SPROP:+4 competence bonus on Knowledge (arcana) checks about the stars, planets or moons, and grants the Astrological Forecasting feat. Faint divination; CL 5th; Craft Wondrous Item, augury. Price 8,300 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.27
Bracelets of Alluvial Stability	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Bracer	COST:30000	WT:0	SPROP:Worn by one of a Graygem race (kender, dwarf and so on), these brass bracelets steady its essence in the River of Time so that it cannot alter the time stream. Moderate abjuration; CL 5th; Craft Wondrous Item, magic circle against chaos. Price 30,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Bracers of River Defense	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Bracer	COST:128280	WT:2	SPROP:Three times a day, generate a selective temporal shield, as the spell. Strong abjuration; CL 13th; Craft Wondrous Item, selective temporal shield. Price 128,280 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Eyes of the Historian	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Eyegear	COST:21600	WT:0	SPROP:Gold-rimmed spectacles: while worn and looking at a person or object whose history you puzzle over, you see its past as with past-seeing, once a day for up to 15 minutes. Moderate divination; CL 15th; Craft Wondrous Item, past-seeing. Price 21,600 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Eyes of the River	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Eyegear	COST:64000	WT:0	SPROP:While worn, a constant river watch with a range of 500 feet; worn more than an hour at a time, it brings on a headache. Even carried and not worn, the owner has a perfect sense of time. Strong divination; CL 8th; Craft Wondrous Item, river watch. Price 64,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Helm of Prescience	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Headgear	COST:43200	WT:2	BONUS:COMBAT|INITIATIVE|2|TYPE=Insight	BONUS:SAVE|Reflex|1|TYPE=Insight	SPROP:Once a day, moment of prescience on the wearer; while worn, +2 insight bonus on initiative checks and +1 insight bonus on Reflex saves. Strong divination; CL 15th; Craft Wondrous Item, moment of prescience. Price 43,200 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Iron Nail of Iteration	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:4000	WT:0	SPROP:Driven into a surface bearing a magical aura, it repeats the spell or spell-like ability (5th level or lower) that made the aura, as if recast by its original caster (resetting an ongoing duration), and tells that caster who drove the nail and where, as a sending. One use; afterward it radiates the repeated spell's aura. Moderate evocation and transmutation; CL 11th; Craft Wondrous Item, lucubration, sending. Price 4,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.28
Ring of Temporal Health	TYPE:Magic.Ring	COST:7050	WT:0	SPROP:On command, casts timeheal on the wearer, restoring his health from any moment up to twenty minutes ago. One use; the pebble burns away. Strong evocation; CL 20th; Forge Ring, timeheal. Price 7,050 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
River's Dagger	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Dagger	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Finesseable.Ranged.Thrown.Simple.Specific.Piercing.Slashing.Dagger	COST:32240	WT:1	DAMAGE:1d4	CRITRANGE:2	CRITMULT:x2	RANGE:10	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|1|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:A +1 dagger with a guardless blade of water-blue crystal. Three times a day, a touch attack with the command word casts frozen moment on a Medium or smaller creature or object; no save is allowed, and the effect lasts 7 rounds. Moderate evocation; CL 7th; Craft Magic Arms and Armor, frozen moment. Price 32,240 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
Sand of Impedance	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:750	WT:0	SPROP:A glass vial of magic sand thrown as a splash weapon (PHB Chapter 8). Creatures hit by the splash make a DC 14 Will save or are affected as by slow; a creature targeted and hit fails automatically. Faint transmutation; CL 5th; Craft Wondrous Item, slow. Price 750 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
Time Candles	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:306000	WT:0	SPROP:Lit, it sheds bright light in a 20-ft. radius and the creature who lit it is under time stop for four hours of its own time (a second or two to anyone else). Stepping outside the 20-ft. radius ends it; moving the candle needs both hands (one to hold it, one to shield the flame), or it goes out. Putting it out ends the spell and ruins the candle. Strong transmutation; CL 17th; Craft Wondrous Item, time stop. Price 306,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29
Dagger of Righteous Vengeance	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Dagger	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Finesseable.Ranged.Thrown.Simple.Specific.Piercing.Slashing.Dagger.Intelligent.Cursed	COST:96302	WT:1	DAMAGE:1d4	CRITRANGE:2	CRITMULT:x2	RANGE:10	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|2|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:Also called the dagger of jealousy: a +2 cursed dagger of venom. Intelligent: AL CE; Int 10, Wis 12, Cha 12; empathy, 30 ft. vision and hearing; Ego 10. Lesser power: 10 ranks in Intimidate (+11 total). Special purpose: defeat or slay those the wielder seeks vengeance against; dedicated power: +2d6 sneak attack and +4 luck bonus on sneak attack rolls. Each day it is owned, the owner makes a DC 10 Will save or shifts one step toward chaotic evil (law-chaos first, then good-evil); when the owner is injured or robbed, it tries to dominate him into harming whoever caused the offense. Strong necromancy; CL 15th; Craft Magic Arms and Armor, bestow curse, inflict moderate wounds, poison. Price 96,302 stl; cost 48,302 stl + 1,920 XP.	SOURCEPAGE:p.120
Device of Time Journeying	TYPE:Artifact.Major	SPROP:Also called the Scepter of Time. A jeweled scepter that folds into a pendant, unfolded and activated by speaking its chant. It carries everyone within 10 feet, always including its user, through time and space; they arrive at the desired time or the desired place, rarely both, unless the user makes a DC 20 Use Magic Device check (+1 per 100 years back, +2 per decade forward). Anyone trying to steal it is affected by antipathy (30th-level wizard); lost or given away, it returns to the last person to activate it. Usable only by the First Races (elves, humans, ogres); a Graygem race using it lets Chaos alter the time stream.	SOURCEPAGE:p.29-30
Globe of Present Time Passing	TYPE:Artifact.Major	SPROP:Also called the Sphere of Time. A flawless floating crystal globe that, touched, fills with moonlight and shows what is happening across Krynn at that moment, each event seen and heard in turn; its owner can also travel to those events in spirit form. Made by Raistlin Majere for Astinus. Rumor says it lets the owner swim upstream into the past, at the risk of his spirit being severed from his body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.30-31
Tapestry of Time	TYPE:Artifact.Minor	SPROP:A gnomish tapestry of a river that shows the future. Once a day, a character who views it for five minutes and makes a DC 20 Wisdom check (no taking 20 until three successful viewings) sees a still image of a likely future event tied to himself or those close to him; it shows the most likely outcome as things stand, and may change as plans change. It never shows the present or the past. Guarded in Mount Nevermind; viewers must first clear the gnomes' bureaucracy.	SOURCEPAGE:p.31
